  "body": "### Summary\n\nThe reader web tests sometimes wait about 240 s for a scroll report that never comes, after a scroll back to the top, and then fail. CI goes red on PRs that did not touch the code.\n\n### Observed\n\n- `ReaderLandingWebTests.aDocumentLandsOnItsAnchor…` (`App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/ReaderWebControllerTests.swift:201`): \"reported: [2]\" after 247 s, in job 133110414600 on #924 head 68d380ef. `reader.js` there is byte-identical to its merge base, and the same test passed in 3.8 s at 51da4c09 (job 133090341114). The log shows WebContent process trouble just before the failure.\n- Probably the same cause: `ReaderPageEndWebTests.aTallPageReportsItsEndOnlyWhenItIsScrolledThere` on #924 (jobs 133066684120 and 133081541823), about 241 s waiting for the report after `window.scrollTo(0, 0)`. That test now moves to #820's own PR.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Find why a scroll report is lost on the simulator: a WebContent process restart, the `scroll` event not firing for a programmatic scroll with no visual change, or reporting that depends on `visualViewport`.\n- Fix the cause in `reader.js` or in the test helper. Never quarantine, skip or loosen a test.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The cause is named with evidence: a log, or a repro with a forced WebContent restart.\n- [ ] 20 consecutive runs of the reader web suites pass on CI, or locally on the Mac.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
